<Page title="Privacy Policy" heading="Privacy" updated="29 October 2026"
  description="How Folio handles your data: nothing leaves your iPhone without an account, and with one your diary is end-to-end encrypted so we can't read it."
  lede="Plain English, because it’s your diary. The short version: we can’t read it.">
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>Folio is made by {site.company.name}, a company registered in England and Wales (company no. {site.company.number}), registered office {site.company.office}. We are the controller of the little personal data described here. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Without an account</h2>
  <p>Everything stays on your iPhone. We receive nothing: no diary content, no usage data, no identifiers.</p>

  <h2>With an account</h2>
  <p>Accounts and sync are coming soon. When you choose to turn them on, we store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your email address and the IDs of the sign-in providers you use (Apple, Google or email), so you can sign in;</li>
    <li>the model and system version of each signed-in device (for example “iPhone 15 Pro · iOS 27.1” or “Chrome on macOS”), when it was added and when it was last seen, so you can manage and sign them out. A name you give a device is end-to-end encrypted like your diary;</li>
    <li>your diary — entries, photos, tasks, categories and settings — <strong>only in end-to-end encrypted form</strong>. It is encrypted on your device with a key only your devices hold. We can’t read it, and we can’t recover it without your devices or your recovery key. Because Apple’s App Store privacy labels have no category for end-to-end encrypted data, our label lists your photos and other diary content as data we collect — it is still only stored in a form we can’t read.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our servers see only what they need to move encrypted data around: record IDs, sizes, version numbers and timestamps.</p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website, our servers, database and storage. Data may be processed anywhere in Cloudflare’s global network.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends sign-in codes by email.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong> and <strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don’t sell or share your data with anyone else, and there is no advertising.</p>

  <h2>Dictation and writing tools</h2>
  <p>Dictation and the ✦ writing tools run on your iPhone using Apple’s on-device models. Audio and text are not sent to us or to anyone else, and audio is never stored.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. The web app, when it launches, will use one strictly necessary cookie to keep you signed in — nothing for analytics or advertising, so there’s no cookie banner.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account data: until you delete your account. Deletion is immediate for you; server clean-up, including backups, finishes within 30 days at most.</li>
    <li>Items you delete in Folio go to <strong>Recently Deleted</strong> on your devices for 30 days, then they’re permanently deleted (sooner if you empty it).</li>
    <li>To stop abuse, sign-in and code requests are counted per network address for up to two days. We store only a keyed hash of the address, never the address itself.</li>
    <li>Support emails: up to 24 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK GDPR and EU GDPR you can ask for access to your data, a copy of it, correction or deletion. The quickest copy is the in-app export (Profile → Your data → Export). You can delete your account in the app or on the web — see <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>. You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>).</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Folio is not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we’ll update the date at the top and, for meaningful changes, tell you in the app.</p>
</Page>
